WEBVTT

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.510
Who's that?

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.260
You there.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.010
This area is for authorized personnel only.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.850
What is this?

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.930
Her world melting is progressing
faster than I thought.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.600
What's happening?

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.010
What happened?

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.510
What?

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.390
Hey, how did--

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.970
This is...

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.640
Hey.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.180
What is this place?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.260
Like I know.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.600
F-For now, stay near me.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.260
Assistant Director Togo, can you hear me?

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.850
Something's wrong here.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.050
What are you doing?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.470
No one told you to get up!

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.550
Chief Hayaseura!

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:03.850
You bastard--

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.300
Mr. Narihisago!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.220
What's going on, sir?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.640
Nothing to worry about.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.220
Stay calm.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.140
Don't!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.680
Sir, what are you doing?

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.800
Arrest him! He's John Walker!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.050
Narihisago Akihito.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:28.760
I truly feel sorry for what
happened to you, including this.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:31.050
But it has to be me

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.550
who kills me!

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:53.760
It's a bit awkward to confess this to you three.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.300
But to tell you the truth,
I've never actually killed anyone.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.640
After all, I'm an officer of the law,

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:08.100
and whether you believe it or not,
I have my own sense of justice.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.260
In accordance with it, I'm going to
turn the Kura into a giant Mizuhanome,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:18.470
so that it can investigate
on a much larger scale.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.050
And then I'll retire.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.350
Momoki can succeed me.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.510
There's no justice in what you've done!

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:33.890
I created the Kura and
caught many serial killers.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:37.550
Sure, I <i>did</i> create some of them.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.680
But as long as the Kura endures,

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.600
my liability will be balanced in no time,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.050
and better outcomes will be obtained.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.720
And so... it is also in recompense...

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.760
...that I kill myself.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:00.850
Dammit!

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:02.680
Some recompense!

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:06.300
He intends to live on in his well
as a brilliant detective!

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.970
Mr. Narihisago, what about your wound?

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.930
It's fine! I'll pursue him even if it kills me!

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.010
Fukuda Tamotsu, come with us!

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.180
What?

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.470
No thanks.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:20.430
Move the body! Come on!

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.390
Fine, fine.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.760
I'm really getting fed up with--

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.800
This is Kaeru.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:02.600
And my name is Uraido.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:07.050
It is I, the brilliant detective,
who will solve the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.970
And it is I who killed her.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:30.180
And the reason this little bitch made it
so easy to solve the mystery and be free

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.220
is that she wants me to see this world's secret.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:42.180
By seeing this face, I remember who I am.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.180
My name is Hayaseura Takuhiko.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.260
And by forcing me to remember my true name,

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.140
the little bitch probably intends
to trap me in a well storm.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:59.050
Too bad for her I'm already dead,
so my id well won't be updating.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.930
Just as I predicted.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:22.850
Thanks to my repeated forays
into Asukai Kiki's mind,

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:26.430
we practically share an unconscious.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:29.260
My id well, the id wells I created,

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:33.510
and the id wells I've never seen
from the unknown serial killers of the world--

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.800
all are laid out in this world.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.390
You heard him.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:43.140
Ms. Kaeru's case is solved. Now what do we do?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.220
Now what? Well...

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:50.180
You brilliant detectives
hiding over there. Do come out.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.010
He saw us?!

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:56.140
It's as if he knew we'd be here.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.260
He vanished.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.510
Mr. Sakaido.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:19.640
Dammit. I don't really want to do this, but...

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:36.140
You.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.180
My, my.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:43.010
Fukuda Tamotsu really isn't here.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.970
Then I have a plan.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.970
He ran? Again?

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:54.760
If that's a property of this world,
any brilliant detective can do it, too.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.890
Wait.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.550
Are you all okay? Any injuries?

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:12.550
No, but... is this... reality?

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.720
It doesn't seem to be, but...

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.800
An id well, perhaps?

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.470
But we've never investigated any such well.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.550
To begin with, only killers
can enter an id well.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:27.720
And we don't appear to have
transformed into brilliant detectives.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:28.970
And we remember.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.140
Nor is Kaeru present.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.680
Asukai Kiki.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.510
She was walking the halls of the Kura.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.970
That's it! If we assume that's
the Mizuhanome's true form...

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:48.350
In other words, the Mizuhanome itself is Asukai Kiki.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:53.050
Then of course the well
within the well would be hers.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:57.180
This is happening because she's
been released from the machine.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:02.510
Remember the incident from the night
she vanished from the hospital...

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.550
The nurses' mass coma incident.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.180
Exactly.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:16.600
Couldn't we all be unconscious and
sharing the same dream, just like them?

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.390
Look!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.890
Boulders?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.050
Maybe they're still far away?

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:33.850
No! We just don't have a point of reference!

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:34.970
Run!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:44.100
Hey, what do you think happens if we die here?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.550
Think we wake up?

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:46.850
Good question!

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:50.680
Four of the thirteen nurses are still in a coma.

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:54.970
So, there's a 69% chance
to wake up! Practically 70%!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.640
Wanna test it?

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:57.970
No, I'll pass!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.350
I don't like my odds!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.140
Director Momoki!

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:16.430
Did the Wellside respond?

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.350
No dice.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.760
No one knows the situation inside.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.720
We only have security footage
from directly after the incident began.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.260
Look.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.760
This is...

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.300
It's happening again!

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.760
Again?! What do you mean?

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.180
It's Ms. Asukai.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:35.140
What? The Challenger victim
you were searching for?

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:40.850
I had suspected she was kidnapped and
used in the development of the Mizuhanome.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:44.390
I never imagined she was under our noses!

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.510
Hey, what the hell is all this?

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:58.970
A Mizuhanome... The entire Kura
has become one giant Mizuhanome!

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.720
Chief Hayaseura.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:06.800
Yeah.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:10.260
He was busy while we were
in shock over the arrest warrant.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.350
Seems he entered his own id well.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:14.720
He must intend to live there.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.430
If he's in a well, we can't get him.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:21.680
In order to quell this situation...

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:26.220
If this phenomenon is due to Asukai Kiki...

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.970
We'll have to shelter her.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:29.970
Shelter?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.140
Like whisk her off to a hospital?

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:33.220
No...

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.430
We'll put her back in the Mizuhanome.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:41.850
There may be no place for her
besides the Mizuhanome.

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.890
But how?

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:44.890
Look!

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.640
We can't get close to her.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.970
If we storm the Kura, we'll end up like them.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:52.550
We'll take countermeasures, of course.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:57.470
The last time this happened,
someone was able to get in and take her.

00:12:57.470 --> 00:13:00.350
After repeated experiments and preparation.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.760
What is this place?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.510
Be careful, Hijiriido!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:12.100
We can't just handle this
with our brilliant detective skills.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.470
That's correct, Ms. Hijiriido.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:26.140
No matter how brilliant you are,
this place's secret is beyond you.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:27.930
So I'll just tell you!

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:31.050
Your name is Hondomachi Koharu.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.640
And this is your id well!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.050
Hijiriido!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:48.390
Follow him! Before you're
caught up in this storm!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.760
Go to the lightning well!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.010
Go and remember!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.600
Who you are,

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:55.680
and what you have to do for the world!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.260
Ouch.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.220
Nice catch.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:43.220
Fukuda Tamotsu?!

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:29.890
Is this it?

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:34.760
Yeah. The helmet that was used
during the nurses' mass coma incident.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:37.720
A prototype Mizuhanome, you might say.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:40.180
We're seizing this as evidence.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.600
B-But!

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.470
Now, let's get going.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:47.010
We don't have a court order, after all.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:48.850
Before we go...

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.140
...commandeer some drugs, too.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.350
Fukuda!

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:05.930
Here I am.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.260
You saved me. Thank you.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:10.850
That's one impressive memory you've got.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.640
You memorized the number of steps to Kaeru?

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.430
I both love and hate numbers.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.350
Now then. What's next?

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:21.430
I'm going after him, of course.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:22.640
What about you?

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.260
I'm not a brilliant detective right now.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.970
I can't keep up with you,
and I have no reason to follow.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:32.720
But I did like your drive to kill.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:35.720
I'd like to spend some more time there.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.470
That kind of creeps me out.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.140
Oh, there's a thought.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:44.640
Since you both love and hate numbers,
how do you feel about seven?

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:49.510
Hmm. It's not a bad number,
but I dislike people who like it.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.180
It's pretentious.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.510
What do you mean?

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:53.970
For just a prime number,

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:57.430
it has all this meaning
and storytelling attached.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:02.010
It's become a number with
an exceedingly nice appearance.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.390
Oh, very interesting.

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:07.260
See ya.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.180
Oh, come on!

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.510
One...

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.470
...hole...

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:28.890
Fukuda?!

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:37.890
I meant to shout, "Here's my chance!" just now.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.720
But it came out all funny, huh.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.010
One hole.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.300
That's very important.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.300
One-track mind.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.010
No dirty jokes.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.300
What?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:56.050
I, uh, that's not what I meant.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.100
Inami Nahoshi!

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.800
Thank you, Hondomachi Koharu.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:13.760
I'm glad I got to save you.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:19.550
I just had two wishes granted.
"Here's my chance!"...

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:26.430
I'm gonna tell you a secret.

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:33.640
I stopped seeing your hole.

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:39.510
When something's missing, or removed,
or fragmented, that's not how I see it.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.800
It looks whole.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:49.010
And so, with Inami Nahoshi,

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.850
that I managed to find her...

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:55.350
...was no coincidence.

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:00.720
In that case...

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:05.550
I didn't get to see what it's like,

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:08.430
but I'm sure you'd like my id well.

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:12.720
Inside of you, my hole is filled...

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:16.140
That makes three wishes granted.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.970
Three...

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.550
A fine number.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:36.680
You killed my man, and I've killed yours.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:39.350
I guess that makes us even.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:42.220
He wasn't my man.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:46.050
After everything, it feels like
my wish will be granted, too.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:50.680
This will let me see Kazuta, right?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:51.970
No, don't!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.300
Kazuta.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.930
Hey, Inami.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.930
You got even prettier.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.850
But you need to hide.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.430
There's a super scary monster.

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:41.260
K-Ka... Ka--

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.930
Kazu--

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.300
Hondomachi.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:17.140
You remembered, didn't you, Mr. Narihisago?

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:18.300
Yeah.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:20.930
Are you okay?

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.600
Yes.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:29.550
Do you think that if we get out of this well,

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:34.050
all the deaths here will be undone?

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:35.430
Who knows.

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:37.390
But I have this feeling

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:41.510
the people who want to live
will come back to life.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:44.470
They have to live.

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:45.680
Yeah.

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:48.720
I'm not going to die here either.

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:49.890
Yeah.

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:54.180
Just wait, cane bastard.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:58.430
The brilliant detectives you made
will send you to true hell.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:00.050
No, that's too dark!

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:03.010
Let's hit him with the spark of life, instead!

00:22:03.010 --> 00:22:04.930
Huh?

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:07.350
Well, let's go with that, then.

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:08.600
Okay!

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:46.600
Sorry.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:48.850
The machine at the chest is too tight.

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:51.550
We couldn't get the size right on short notice.

00:23:51.550 --> 00:23:52.720
It's fine.

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.930
We'll be monitoring your vitals
and other info from here.

00:23:56.930 --> 00:24:00.470
The same info will appear
on the display on your helmet.

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:02.970
Okay. Understood.

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:06.510
Momoki.

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:10.510
What if she refuses to be
put back in the Mizuhanome?

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:19.470
I... have to protect the lives
of my subordinates.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.430
Take command, Mr. Matsuoka.

00:24:24.430 --> 00:24:26.050
Got it.

00:24:26.050 --> 00:24:27.720
Go get it done.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:29.430
See you again soon.
